diff --git a/pillow/src/mission-runtime/PERSISTENCE.md b/pillow/src/mission-runtime/PERSISTENCE.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..58116497
--- /dev/null
+++ b/pillow/src/mission-runtime/PERSISTENCE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Mission state recovery
+
+The hosted Pillow session stores Mission Runtime state beside the configured
+Brain database, at `<DATABASE_PATH>.missions.json`. Standalone in-process tests
+may omit this file; production session startup refuses a missing or in-memory
+database path. This file must be included in private backups with the database.
+
+A successful mission mutation waits for file sync, atomic replacement and POSIX
+directory sync. Creation and lifecycle transitions include their history in the
+same snapshot. Mission records, transitions, checkpoints, retries, recovery,
+reports and audit history reload before the runtime initializes. Loading does
+not call workers or grant new approval: the recorded structural status and
+approval values remain unchanged. This is persistence of the structural mission
+runtime, not proof that an underlying real mission executed or that Birth or
+commerce is authorized.
+
+Snapshot corruption, an unsupported version, a conflicting writer, write failure
+or the 16 MiB capacity limit fails closed; history is never silently truncated or
+reset. Failed writes are not acknowledged as successful mutations. A failure
+after atomic replacement can leave an unacknowledged state on disk; reconciliation
+and reload are required rather than guessing whether that mutation succeeded.
+
+Writers use an exclusive short-lived `.lock` file and verify the last loaded
+snapshot fingerprint under that lock. A crashed write may leave a lock. Preserve
+the snapshot and reconcile the exclusive writer before removing a stale lock;
+the runtime does not guess that a lock belonging to another container is stale.
+Orphan `.tmp` files are not used for recovery. Windows does not receive the POSIX
+directory-sync guarantee. This change does not establish multi-service mission
+execution, automatic replay, transactionality with external effects or independent
+production restart certification.
